# IDSC — environment variable examples
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and fill in real values locally.
# NEVER commit real values, API keys, passwords or service-role keys to git.
# .env* files are git-ignored on purpose.

# --- Application ---
# Public URL of the deployed app (used for links in notifications/receipts)
# VITE_APP_URL=http://localhost:8080

# --- Database / backend (Lovable Cloud / Supabase-compatible) ---
# Configured automatically when Lovable Cloud is enabled; listed here so the
# project can also run against a self-hosted instance outside Lovable.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
# Server-only — never expose to the browser, never commit:
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- Payments (Paystack initially; manual cash/EFT recorded by staff) ---
# Server-only secrets:
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# Paystack webhook signatures use PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY (no separate webhook key).
# VITE_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_...

# --- AI assistant (English only for now; truthful, localised answers) ---
# Configured via the Lovable AI Gateway when enabled; no key needed in repo.

# M02: every variable above is optional and commented out. No services enabled.
# Never prefix private credentials with VITE_; that exposes them in the browser.
# Deployment details: docs/DEPLOYMENT.md. Backup plan: docs/BACKUP_RESTORE.md.
